# Single-page-app routing is handled by wrangler.jsonc, not from here.
#
# react-router-dom needs every path to serve index.html, or a hard refresh on
# e.g. /designer/opportunities/:id 404s. On Cloudflare Workers that is
# `assets.not_found_handling: "single-page-application"` in wrangler.jsonc.
#
# The old rule here — `/*  /index.html  200` — is REJECTED by Workers with
# "Infinite loop detected" [code: 100324]: Workers rewrites /index.html back
# to /, which re-matches /* forever. Cloudflare Pages accepted the same rule,
# so restore it only if this app is ever moved back to Pages. Netlify has its
# own copy in netlify.toml; Vercel's is in vercel.json.
#
# This file is kept, without rules, so the absence of a rewrite here is
# deliberate rather than an oversight. public/_headers still carries the
# no-cache rules for the service worker and the manifest.
